                <pb facs="0471" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11796: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-17T14:00:00+08:00">February 17, 1932—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 17—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>238. Following from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“February 16, 6 p.m. Today’s press reports state that Hsi Chia from Kirin, and Chang Ching-hui from Harbin, arrived at
                            Mukden yesterday and Ma Chan-shan
                            here today. The long-delayed conference in regard to the denunciations
                                [<hi rendition="#italic">declaration?</hi>] of the new state is
                            scheduled to open on the 17th or 18th and one Japanese press report
                            makes the definite statement that the state will be declared before
                            February 25th.</p>
                        <p>Apparently this movement is being energetically pushed by interested
                            parties at this time and judging from appearances early developments are
                            to be expected.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
